        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: தற்காலிக",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தற்காலிக — taṟkālika — \"temporary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "இது ஒரு தற்காலிக வேலை, மூன்று மாதங்கள் மட்டுமே. itu oru taṟkālika vēlai, mūṉṟu mātaṅkaḷ maṭṭumē. This is a temporary job, only for three months."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It stands before a noun. As an adverb: தற்காலிகமாக, for the time being."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தற்காலிக (taṟkālika) is borrowed from a Sanskrit adjective built on tatkāla, \"happening at that same time, immediately\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
